# ESLint Config Building Code

**The `toWarns` function definition:**
```javascript
function toWarns(config) {
  if (!config) return config;
  if (!Array.isArray(config) && typeof config[Symbol.iterator] === "function") {
    return [...config].map(toWarns);
  }
  if (Array.isArray(config)) return config.map(toWarns);
  const result = { ...config };
  if (result.extends) result.extends = toWarns(result.extends);
  if (result.rules) {
    result.rules = Object.fromEntries(
      Object.entries(result.rules).map(([key, value]) => {
        if (key.startsWith("eslint-comments/")) return [key, value];
        if (value === "error" || value === 2) return [key, "warn"];
        if (Array.isArray(value) && (value[0] === "error" || 
            value[0] === 2)) return [key, ["warn", ...value.slice(1)]];
        return [key, value];
      })
    );
  }
  return result;
}
```

**Application to obsidianmd config:**
The function spreads and maps: `...toWarns(obsidianmd.configs.recommended)` — this recreates objects via the spread operator `{ ...config }` and `Object.fromEntries()`.

**Full ESLint invocation:**
```javascript
'npx', [
  '--prefix', scannerDir, 'eslint', '--config', configPath,
  '--format', 'json', '--no-error-on-unmatched-pattern', '.'
]
```
With `cwd: workspacePath` and environment variable `NODE_PATH` joining scanner and workspace `node_modules`.

